            "title": "Incorrect assignment of mountapp.mountpath in app.use",
            "severity": "high",
            "file": "lib/application.js",
            "line": 171,
            "explanation": "The line 'mount_app.mountpath = path;' assigns the entire 'path' argument, which may be undefined or a function, to mount_app.mountpath. The correct variable holding the mount path is 'mount_path'. This causes sub-applications to have incorrect or undefined mountpath values after being mounted.",
            "suggestion": "Change 'mount_app.mountpath = path;' to 'mount_app.mountpath = mount_path;' to properly assign the mount path.",
            "failureAfterChange": "When mounting a sub-application using app.use('/foo', subapp), subapp.mountpath is incorrectly set to a function or undefined (the argument 'path'), not the string '/foo'. For example, accessing subapp.mountpath will not return '/foo', causing errors in routing or path resolution related to the sub-application's mount path.",
            "alreadyFixedByChange": true
          }
